# A single-node Redis with cluster mode ENABLED. This is not a sharded cluster
# and needs no routing: one node owning all 16384 slots is enough to test the
# cluster-safe-keys feature, because Redis checks that a multi-key command's
# keys share a slot BEFORE it considers which node owns that slot. It also
# answers CLUSTER KEYSLOT, which a non-cluster instance refuses, so the CRC16
# implementation can be differential-tested against the server itself.
#
# The test suite assigns the slots in beforeAll via CLUSTER ADDSLOTSRANGE.
#
# The announce settings matter for any *cluster-aware client* (an
# ioredis.Cluster, say) rather than a plain connection: such a client reads
# CLUSTER SLOTS and then dials whatever host/port it finds there. Without
# these it finds the in-container 6379 and connects to something else
# entirely, or nothing. They hard-code the documented `-p 6381:6379` mapping
# below, so run the container on that port or override them.
FROM redis:8-alpine

EXPOSE 6379

CMD ["redis-server", \
  "--cluster-enabled", "yes", \
  "--save", "", \
  "--appendonly", "no", \
  "--cluster-announce-ip", "127.0.0.1", \
  "--cluster-announce-port", "6381", \
  "--cluster-announce-bus-port", "16381"]
